Part C — Dock / marina boats, weather / ocean audio, build-time AI Studio tools
1. Dock / marina arrival (server-authoritative)
The pre-match space is a dock/marina, not a void or an instant spawn on the island. Players gather on the dock, board their team’s boat, then sail to their side of the island. Build the marina and boats from Kenney Pirate Kit dock/boat pieces (see Part B).

Room phase is server-authoritative and advances only: dock → boarding → sailing → landing → match → (existing) ended. Durations, dock bounds, slip poses, boat speed, and landingRadius are named ENGINE constants. Invalid phase values fail closed. The server must not skip a phase (no jump from dock to sailing).
A shared marina (static, from checked-in config / named ENGINE marina pose — not a team base) has one slip and one boat per team. Use Pirate Kit docks and boats, muted PBR, team color only on trim/banners.
dock: the room starts here. Players spawn and may move only on the dock (server clamps to named dock bounds). They are not on the island and not on a boat yet (landed === false, boatId empty).
boarding: players board their team’s boat at that team’s slip (interact and/or auto-board at the end of ENGINE.boardingDurationSec). boatId is set; landed stays false. The server does not advance to sailing until every non-helper player who is in the room is on their own team’s boat.
sailing: boats leave the marina along a deterministic path that ends at that team’s base shore (the shoreline in front of that team’s radial base — 2π * i / teamCount — not the shared marina and not an enemy beach).
landing: the boat is at the end of the path and players disembark onto land on their own side (landed === true, boatId cleared).
Base-helper NPCs may already be at their base and do not block “all have landed.” Roaming bots board and sail with their team if they arrive by boat.
The match clock (matchTimeRemaining) starts decrementing only when all have landed (every non-helper player who was present at the start of sailing has landed === true) and phase is match. Until then it stays at ENGINE.matchDurationSec. Combat, crate opens, and building are rejected until match (fail closed). Do not break AT-17’s evaluateMatchEnd unit tests; just don’t tick the timer or open the match early.
The client only renders the marina, boats, and seats; it does not author phase, boat pose, boarding, or landing.
2. Weather and ocean audio (visual / audio only)
The server owns weather on the room state: kind is only clear | overcast | rain | storm. wind, fogDensity, and rainIntensity are required numbers inside named ENGINE min/max. A default starting kind is a named ENGINE constant (e.g. defaultWeatherKind), not an invented ad-hoc value. The server may change weather within those bounds (named hold/transition times if you add a cycle).
The client presents weather only: rain particles, wind on foliage/camera, fog density, and optional sky exposure. No gameplay effect this pass — no movement slow, no damage, no accuracy or visibility rule changes.
Positional ocean / wave ambience via the Web Audio API, gain (and optional low-pass) scaled by distance from the listener (local predicted pose) to the shoreline, using named ENGINE constants. Louder at the beach, quieter inland. Buffers come from the manifest (CC0 and/or AI Studio generated at build time). Missing buffers fail closed unless audio is explicitly off.
